# Protect SafeSakay database (local MySQL)

The app uses **MySQL `safesakayvue`** for real demo data (orgs, boats, trips, bookings, users). **Do not erase it.**

## Forbidden unless the user explicitly asks in chat to reset or restore the database

- `php artisan migrate:fresh`, `migrate:refresh`, `migrate:reset`, `db:wipe`, `schema:drop`
- One-off debug scripts that call `migrate:fresh` or `db:wipe`
- Any `db:seed --class=Restore*` or `storage/scripts/restore-demo-from-snapshots.php`

`.env` blocks these while `ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_DB=false` and `ALLOW_RESTORE_SCRIPTS=false` (even if the user said "code only" in an older message).

## Safe alternatives

- Run tests: `php artisan test` (uses **SQLite in-memory** via `phpunit.xml`, not MySQL)
- UI/backend changes: edit code only; no DB reset
- Restore demo from snapshots: `php storage/scripts/restore-demo-from-snapshots.php` (adds data; does not wipe)
- Full backup before risky work: `php storage/scripts/backup-database.php` → `storage/backups/`

## If the user truly needs a clean schema

Tell them to run `migrate:fresh` **themselves** in an interactive terminal, or set `ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_DB=true` in `.env` temporarily. Default is **false** so the agent cannot wipe data silently.
